Hi Lauri,

Before the logs - something that's been bugging me. For my setup, if I 
plug the mouse into a kernel with no Solaar and nothing else running,it 
scrolls fast, almost unusable. Only after I disable hi-res in Solaar 
does it scroll normally. So I don't think the test resultsbelow are 
really showing what you wanted to see, since the test starts from a 
state (no Solaar) that's already "broken" for me tobegin with. Sending 
them anyway since you asked for them.

Did the full 4-run test:
- Userspace HID++ tools off (Solaar autostart disabled, nothing else 
running)
- Wheel in ratchet/clicky mode for the whole test, including the 
continuous-scroll part
- Same steps every run: 10 single clicks down (~2s apart), 10 
singleclicks up, then ~5s continuous scroll one direction
- Same browser (Rambox, which is Electron 43.0.0 / 
Chromium 150.0.7871.46 under the hood) - also happens the same way 
inLibreWolf (Firefox-based)
- Receiver unplug/replug + mouse wake before each run

Logs attached:
- evtest-run1-buggy.log - stock module (f0866517be93 present), 
rightafter a fresh reboot
- evtest-run2-fixed.log - reverted module, swapped in live 
(rmmod/insmod) on the same boot, no reboot
- evtest-run3-buggy.log - stock module again, swapped in live
- evtest-run4-fixed.log - reverted module again, swapped in live

Subjectively all four felt fast, consistent with each other - again,none 
had Solaar running so all start from the hi-res default, whichalready 
feels fast to me regardless of the bug.

FYI, not part of these 4 runs: earlier while swapping modules live 
andtoggling hi-res on/off through Solaar, I hit a state where 
scrollingbecame extremely slow instead of fast - matching what your 
original commit message describes. Only happened once, during 
livemodule-swapping + hi-res toggling, never after a plain reboot.

Thanks
Frantisek

